---
title: "pi-run: one run of an id"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  s0: no run
  s1: queued
  s2: running
  s3: exited, done wake
  s4: exited, failed wake
  s5: exited, no wake
  s6: queued after a 429
  s7: lost
  s8: collected
  s9: queued for its PR's red CI
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: pi-run queue #60;id>
  s0 --> s2: pi-run #60;id> #60;role> #60;brief>, or the hourly drain
  s1 --> s2: pi-run #60;id> #60;role> #60;brief>, or the hourly drain
  s2 --> s4: pi exits rc != 0 or pi stops on an upstream 429 [resume.cap spent, sends the failed wake]
  s2 --> s5: pi exits rc 0 [no wake: finish]
  s2 --> s6: pi stops on an upstream 429 [resumes left, frees its slot]
  s2 --> s7: KILL or OOM
  s2 --> s3: pi exits rc 0 [brief has wake: finish]
  s3 --> s8: pi-run collect #60;id>
  s4 --> s8: pi-run collect #60;id>
  s5 --> s8: pi-run collect #60;id>
  s6 --> s2: hourly drain, after resume_at [same session]
  s7 --> s8: pi-run collect #60;id> [sends the failed wake]
  s8 --> s9: its PR is red after the rerun, at a head it pushed [fix attempts left]
  s9 --> s2: hourly drain, after resume_at [same session]
